              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Carqueville"} Nils Carqueville
                (University of Vienna):
              %p
                %strong Truncated Rozansky-Witten models as extended defect TQFTs
              %p
                slides:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.carqueville.net/nils/RW.pdf"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Carqueville-RW.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.03284"} arXiv:2201.03284
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bwDJSitenVE"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  According to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
                  with singularities, fully
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+topological+quantum+field+theories"} extended topological quantum field theories
                  with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defect+QFT"} defects
                  are equivalently described in terms of coherent full duality data for objects and (higher) morphisms as well as appropriate
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fixed+point"} homotopy fixed point
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures"} structures
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rozansky-Witten+theory"} Rozansky-Witten models
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilka+Brunner"} Ilka Brunner
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.theorie.physik.uni-muenchen.de/MATH/members/asc/sci_mem/fragkos_pantelis/index.html"} Pantelis Fragkos
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Roggenkamp"} Daniel Roggenkamp
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#DebrayMar2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arun+Debray"} Arun Debray
                (Purdue University):
              %p
                %strong
                  Twisted string bordism and a potential anomaly in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8 \times E_8
                  heterotic string theory
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.04911"} arXiv:2210.04911
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wkucLJ7jTlM"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} Quantum field theories
                  can have an inconsistency called an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} anomaly
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+field+theory"} invertible field theory
                  in one dimension higher. Theorems of Freed-Hopkins-Teleman and
                  %a{:href => "invertible+field+theory#FreedHopkins21"} Freed-Hopkins
                  classify
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+field+theories"} invertible field theories
                  in terms of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+groups"} bordism groups
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8 \times E_8
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+field+theories"} invertible field theories
                  does not vanish, and therefore there could be an anomaly in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8 \times E_8
                  heterotic string theory. Standard computational techniques for twisted
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+bordism"} string bordism
                  do not work for this problem; I will also discuss work joint with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Yu"} Matthew Yu
                  using Baker-Lazarev’s R-module
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
                  to simplify a large class of twisted spin and string bordism computations.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#YoungMar2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Young"} Matthew Young
                (Utah State University):
              %p
                %strong
                  Non-semisimple TFT and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1 \vert 1)
                  Chern-Simons theory
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.04286"} arXiv:2210.04286
                and
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Chern-Simons+theory"} super Chern-Simons theory
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Young-at-QFTAndCobordism2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m73KQCwXOrY"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"}> Chern-Simons theory
                  , as
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "Chern-Simons+theory#Witten89"} introduced by Witten
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
                  associated to a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+group"} simple Lie group
                  and a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+%28Chern-Simons+theory%29"} level
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theory"} topological field theory
                  was introduced by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Reshetikhin and Turaev
                  and is at the core of modern
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+topology"} quantum topology
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+category"} semisimple
                  modification of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} construction of Reshetikhin and Turaev
                  which realizes Chern-Simons theory with gauge
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1\vert 1)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+category"} modular structure
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+group"} quantum group
                  of
