            %br/
          %ul
            %li#BlanchetMar2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Blanchet"} Christian Blanchet
                (Université Paris Cité):
              %p
                %strong Heisenberg homologies of surface configurations
              %p
                cf.:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08614"} arXiv:2306.08614
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.11475"} arXiv:2206.11475
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Blanchet-at-QFTAndCobordism2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=prcU4v7LFZQ"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer+Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
                  of its one-dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} homology
                  associated with the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection+pairing"} intersection cocycle
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+representation"} representation
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
                  defines
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+coefficients"} local coefficients
                  on the unordered
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
                  in the surface. We study the corresponding
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} homologies
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} Mapping Class Group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} action
                  and the connection with quantum constructions. This is based on joint work with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Awais+Shaukat"} Awais Shaukat
