                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Palmer"} Martin Palmer
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#ChbiliMar2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nafaa+Chbili"} Nafaa Chbili
                (United Arab Emirates University):
              %p
                %strong Quasi-alternating links, Examples and obstructions
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.08624"} arXiv:2009.08624
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1hd0vFxU2ro"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Quasi-alternating links represent an important class of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/links"} links
                  that has been
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309170"} introduced by Ozsváth and Szabó
                  while studying the Heegaard Floer homology of the branched double-covers of alternating links. This new class of links, which share many
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Khovanov+homology"} homological properties
                  with alternating links, is defined in a recursive way which is not easy to use in order to determine whether a given link is quasi-alternating. In this talk, we shall review the main obstruction criteria for quasi-alternating links. We also discuss how new examples of quasi-alternating links can constructed.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#QazaqzehMar2023
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://math.sci.kuniv.edu.kw/people/faculty/khaled-qazaqezeh"} Khaled Qazaqzeh
                (Kuwait University):
              %p
                %strong On the Finiteness of Quasi-alternating Links
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.02984"} arXiv:2208.02984
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Qazaqzeh-at-QFTAndCobordism2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bUsCDAUiX60"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p The generalization of alternating links to quasi-alternating links raises some natural questions that have affirmative answer in the class of alternating links.
                %p In this talk, we discuss these questions and then we give an affirmative answer to one question without any assumption. As a consequence, we prove that one of these questions is solved in the affirmative iff Green’s conjecture on the finiteness of quasi-alternating links of a given determinant holds. Also, we prove that another question is solved in the affirmative implies Green’s conjecture on the finiteness of quasi-alternating links of a given determinant holds.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#PavlovMar2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Pavlov"} Dmitri Pavlov
                (Texas Tech University):
              %p
                %strong The geometric cobordism hypothesis
              %p
                cf.:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.01208"} arXiv:2011.01208
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.01095"} arXiv:2111.01095
              %p
                slides:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://dmitripavlov.org/nyuad.pdf"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Pavlov-GCHatCQTS.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n6Eog_z82eA"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  I will explain my recent joint work with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Grady"} Daniel Grady
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field+theory"} locality
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+field+theories"} functorial field theories
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.01208"}> arXiv:2011.01208
                  ) and the
                  %a{:href => "cobordism+hypothesis#ReferencesGeometricCobordisms"} geometric cobordism hypothesis
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.01095"}> arXiv:2111.01095
                  ). The latter generalizes the Baez–Dolan
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
                  to non-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theories"}> topological field theories
                  , in which
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordisms"} bordisms
                  can be equipped with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometric
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures"} structures
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+maps"} smooth maps
                  to a fixed
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} manifold
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metrics"} Riemannian metrics
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+structures"} conformal structures
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} with connection
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+string+structures"} geometric string structures
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "cobordism+category#GMTWTheorem"} Galatius–Madsen–Tillmann–Weiss theorem
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/What+is+an+elliptic+object%3F"} conjecture of Stolz and Teichner
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representability
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance+classes"} concordance classes
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+field+theories"} functorial field theories
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+operations"} power operations
                  on the level of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+field+theory"} field theories
                  (extending the
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.09943"} recent work of Barthel-Berwick-Evans-Stapleton
                %p
                  I will illustrate the general theory by constructing the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
                  as a
