                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
                  of field theories in the setting of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "cobordism+hypothesis#ReferencesGeometricCobordisms"} geometric cobordism hypothesis
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#GradyMar2023
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Grady"} Daniel Grady
                (Wichita State University):
              %p
                %strong Deformation classes of invertible field theories and the Freed-Hopkins conjecture
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Grady-at-QFTAndCobordism2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PzD6IDeLlS4"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  In their
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.06527"} seminal paper
                  %a{:href => "#FreedHopkins21"} Freed and Hopkins
                  proved a classification theorem that identifies
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation"} deformation
                  classes of certain
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible+field+theory"} invertible
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theories"} topological field theories
                  with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion subgroup
                  of some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology
                  of a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjectured
                  that the identification continues to hold for non-topological field theories, if one passes from the torsion subgroup to the full
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology group
                  of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Pavlov"} Dmitri Pavlov
                  on the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "cobordism+hypothesis#ReferencesGeometricCobordisms"} geometric cobordism hypothesis
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#BerwickEvansMar23
