                  from those which are not by so-called swampland conjecture. As a consequence of the absence of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+symmetries"} global symmetries
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} QG
                  %a{:href => "swampland#SwamplandCobordismConjecture"} one such conjecture
                  is saying that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+group"} cobordism group
                  has to vanish. In mathematics very often these groups do not vanish right away. Physics tells us that this can be ameliorated by either
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetry"} gauging
                  or
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+breaking"} breaking
                  of the corresponding global symmetries.
                %p
