          %h2#CQTSColloquium Quantum Colloquium
          %p
            Weekly colloquium, broadly on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+systems"} quantum systems
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
            and specifically on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+computation"} topological quantum computation
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependently typed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+languages"} quantum programming languages
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#may_2022 May 2022
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                on joint work with
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %p#CQTSColloquiumCohomotopyFoundationsForTDA
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/New+Foundations+for+TDA+--+Cohomotopy"} New Foundations for Topological Data Analysis – The Power of Cohomotopy
              %p
                %br/
              %blockquote
                %p
                  The aim of
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
                  (TDA) is to provide qualitative analysis of large data/parameter sets in a way which is
                  %em robust
                  against uncertainties and noise. This is accomplished using tools and theorems from the mathematical field of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+homology"} persistent homology
                  has become the signature method of TDA, it tends to produce answers that are either hard to interpret (persistent
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycles"} cycles
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well+groups"} well groups
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "persistent+cohomotopy#FranekKrcal17"} FK17
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                  which we may call
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+cohomotopy"} persistent cohomotopy
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "persistent+cohomotopy#FranekKrcalWagner18"} FKW18
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                  that this new method provides computable answers to the concrete question of detecting whether there exist data+parameters that meet a prescribed target indicator precisely, even in the presence of uncertainty and noise. More generally, efficient data analysis will require further refining
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+cohomotopy"} persistent cohomotopy
                  to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomotopy"} equivariant cohomotopy
                  and/or
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomotopy"} twisted cohomotopy
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Proper+Orbifold+Cohomology"} SS20
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomotopy+theory"} cohomotopy theory
                  have
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} profound relations
                  to formal
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/high+energy+physics"} high energy physics
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} quantum materials
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
          %p
