              %p
                video:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://nyu.zoom.us/rec/play/YTjIGL-Bevb1H44UuL-ZimXdxph5cffddWpP3H4ZsuRT2xu3OrnTbC0NZLsKedUGwS68DJ8onVFPAETb.rreoi7Wt6uXFyaYN?continueMode=true&_x_zm_rtaid=e0VPIMlfT9KlVd_wiaOq6A.1669794985784.11f8cd37091ebf6bdd2a878668e26cd6&_x_zm_rhtaid=404"} rec
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wceg7E1p5Kg"} YT
              %p
                cf.:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "nuclear+magnetic+resonance#SpinResonanceQBitsReferences"} spin resonance qbits
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin"} Spins
                  are a purely
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanical
                  phenomenon and have been proposed as one of the several candidates for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qubits"} qubits
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information science
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computer"} Quantum computers
                  based on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin"} spin
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qubits"} qubits
                  were first
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "quantum+computation#DiVincenzo00"} proposed by DiVincenzo
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computer"} quantum computer
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+magnetic+resonance"} nuclear
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spins"} spins
                  and the theory of spin-spin and spin-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic field
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions"} interactions
                  are well developed, but a quantum computer based on spin qubits has not yet been realized. Why is this?
                %p
                  In this talk, I will discuss the challenges in developing spin qubits that meet
                  %a{:href => "quantum+computation#DiVincenzo00"} DiVincenzo’s criteria
                  for
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computers"} quantum computers
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic field
                  that form the building block of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic+gates"} quantum logic gates
          %p
