              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sophia+Economou"} Sophia Economou
                (Center for Quantum Information Science and Engineering, Virginia Tech, USA)
              %p
                %strong Control and distribution of entanglement in quantum networks
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.10820"} arXiv:2212.10820
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V5pYJLBvNJs"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+network"} Quantum networks
                  are pursued as a quantum backbone on which to perform secure
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+communication"} quantum communication
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+sensing"} quantum sensing
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+repeaters"} quantum repeaters
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/photon"} photonic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information"} quantum information
                  carriers are generated and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correction"} error corrected
                  through
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions"} interactions
                  with matter
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qubits"} qubits
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin"} spin
                  qubits can increase the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+entanglement"} entanglement
                  distribution rate over the network. Specifically, I will describe our recent work on the accurate and fast control of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NMR"} nuclear spin
                  memory qubits coupled to spin defects such as the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NV+center"} NV center
                  in diamond. I will also discuss the deterministic generation of photonic ‘graph“ states from such quantum emitters.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#SaleemApr2023
              %p 10 Apr 2023
              %p Zain Saleem (Argonne National Lab, USA)
              %p
                %strong Classical simulators as quantum error mitigators via circuit cutting
              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.07335"} arXiv:2212.07335
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hOluuHpU-aY"} YT
              %blockquote
                %p
                  We introduce an error mitigation framework that mitigates errors in a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuit"} quantum circuit
                  using circuit cutting. Our framework can be implemented in polynomial time for a wide variety of quantum circuits. Our technique involves cutting the circuit in such a way that we run the circuit that needs to be executed on the quantum hardware whereas the error mitigation circuit is run on a simulator. We perform error mitigation qubit by qubit and then provide a way to combine the different probabilities from each of the individual qubit error mitigation runs such that the full circuit is error mitigated. We apply our framework to the VQE hardware-efficient ansatz acheiving estimated ground state energies very close to the noise-free simulation results.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li
