                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleus"} nuclear
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spins
                  necessitates a quantum leap in sensitivity. My research endeavors to achieve this leap through Pulsed Dynamic Nuclear Polarization (DNP), an emerging technique that harnesses quantum-controlled
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
                  spins to hyperpolarize nuclear spins, overcoming inherent sensitivity challenges in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+magnetic+resonance"} Nuclear Magnetic Resonance
                  (NMR) spectroscopy.
                %p
