              %p
                cf.:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.13374"} arXiv:1904.13374
              %blockquote
                %p
                  Majorana fermions are fermions that were originally proposed in particle physics by Ettore Majorana and are characterized as being their own anti-particle. In condensed matter systems, Majorana quasiparticles occur as fractionalized excitations with an associated topologically protected degeneracy. In this talk, I will briefly review the basic concepts and recent developments in the study of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+zero+modes"} Majorana zero modes
                  in semiconductor-superconductor nanowires and
                  = succeed "-based" do
