                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G'
                  forming a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reductive+dual+pair"} dual pair
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(W)
                %p
                  In his wonderful paper “Remarks on classical invariant theory”, Roger Howe suggested that his classical duality should be extendable to superalgebras/supergroups. In a recent work with Hadi Salmasian, we obtained a classification of irreducible reductive dual pairs in a real or complex orthosymplectic Lie supergroup
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
