              %blockquote
                %p
                  video:
                  %a{:href => "https://nyu.zoom.us/rec/play/-h0SvD8ppAUvJ0zLbko2tUaGWyEK6O3OSNTtUfCBC2L74t4KyphBnpxTz8Wms1jNfKjXj3LlJB8vs-n8.-r0ZCtHR_F__Xa6w?canPlayFromShare=true"} Zm
                %p
                  In this talk, I will explain my works with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"} Y. Tachikawa
                  to study
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} anomalies
                  in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
                  via
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} Topological Modular Forms
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TMF"}> TMF
                  ). TMF is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
                  which is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/What+is+an+elliptic+object%3F"} conjectured by Stolz-Teichner
                  to classify
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-dimensional+Euclidean+field+theory"} two-dimensional supersymmetric quantum field theories
                  in physics. In the previous work &amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.13542"}> arXiv:2108.13542
                  \&amp;rbrack;, we proved the vanishing of anomalies in heterotic string theory mathematically using TMF. Additionally, we have a recent update on the previous work &amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.06196"}> arXiv:2305.06196
                  \&amp;rbrack;. Due to the vanishing result, we can consider a secondary transformation of spectra, which coincides with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anderson+duality"} Anderson self-duality
                  morphism of TMF. This allows us to detect subtle torsion phenomena in TMF by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential-geometric
                  methods.
