                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+twisted+K-theory"} equivariant twisted K-theory
                  provides an even finer invariant. Equivariant twists over
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
                  gained increasing importance in the subject due to a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loop+Groups+and+Twisted+K-Theory"} result by Freed, Hopkins and Teleman
                  that relates the corresponding K-groups to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+ring"} Verlinde ring
                  of the associated
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group"} loop group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  only a small
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
