              %blockquote
                %p
                  In the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} Standard Model
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sterile+neutrino"} sterile right-handed
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrino"} neutrino
                  number
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi vR
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_{vR}
                  is not equal to the family number
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_f
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi f
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi vR
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-N_f + n_{vR})
                  had been advocated to play an important role in the previous work on
                  %em Cobordism and Deformation Class of the Standard Model
                  \&amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.14765"}> arxiv:2112.14765
                  ,
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.08393"} arxiv:2204.08393
                  %em Ultra Unification
                  \&amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.15860"}> arXiv:2012.15860
                  \&amp;rbrack;, in order to predict new highly
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+entanglement"} entangled
                  sectors beyond the Standard Model. Ultra Unification would combine the Standard Model and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} Grand Unification
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+spinor"} Weyl fermions
                  per family, without the necessity of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sterile+neutrino"} right-handed sterile neutrinos
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} topological phase
                  sectors (in 4d or 5d) or new gapless interacting
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal
                  sectors (in 4d) consistent with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonperturbative+effect"} nonperturbative
                  global
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} anomaly cancellation
                  and cobordism constraints (especially from the mixed gauge-gravitational anomaly, such as a
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 16
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_{16}
                  class anomaly, associated with the baryon minus
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lepton"} lepton
                  number B−L and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electroweak+field"} electroweak
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercharge"} hypercharge
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+charge"} current
                  conservation can be violated quantum mechanically by gravitational backgrounds such as gravitational instantons, hypothetically pertinent for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leptogenesis"} leptogenesis
                  in the very early
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} universe
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+global+symmetry"} noninvertible categorical
                  counterpart of the B−L symmetry still survives in gravitational backgrounds. In general, we construct noninvertible symmetry charge operators as topological
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defect+field+theory"} defects
                  derived from invertible anomalous symmetries that suffer from mixed
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitational+anomalies"} gravitational anomalies
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 16
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_{16}
                  respectively. For this construction, we utilize the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+inflow"} anomaly inflow
                  concept, the 4d
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+class"} Pontryagin class
                  and the gravitational
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons 3-form
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Witten-Reshetikhin-Turaev-type
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theory"} topological quantum field theory
                  with a framing anomaly corresponding to a 2d
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+conformal+field+theory"} rational conformal field theory
                  with an appropriate chiral
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+charge"} central charge
                  = succeed "^{TF}-" do
