                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Ibort"} Alberto Ibort
                (Universidad Carlos III of Madrid, Spain)
              %p
                %strong The groupoid picture of Quantum Mechanics
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Ibort-CQTS-Apr2025.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                video:
                %a{:href => "https://nyu.zoom.us/rec/share/wpxjPBiUAMt5oTdBwgD39RvzzjvcMvnD5DsQ8A1cF5_QaBWO5HGAWcS4IOi7TPwV.9i7MJDWMkmQ8qM7E"} zm
              %p
                cf.
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.09326"} arXiv:2002.09326
              %blockquote
                %p
                  The
                  %a{:href => "quantum+observable#ReferencesQuantumObservableAlgebrasAsGroupoidAlgebras"} groupoid picture of Quantum Mechanics
                  is the formal expression of
                  %a{:href => "quantum+observable#Schwinger1969"} Schwinger’s conceptualisation
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+Bohr"} Bohr
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Werner+Heisenberg"} Heisenberg
                  on the fundamental role played by physical transitions in the description of quantum phenomena. In this talk we will review some of the fundamental notions leading to this picture and will discuss some applications regarding the dynamical description of quantum theories.
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#NivesvivatApr2025
              %p 30 Apr 2025
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rongvoram+Nivesvivat"} Rongvoram Nivesvivat
                (NYUAD):
              %p
                %strong Three-point connectivities of interfaces in 2D critical statistical models.
              %p
                slides:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Nivesvivat-CQTS-Apr2025.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                cf.:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.17558"} arXiv:2311.17558
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.08168"} arXiv:2302.08168
              %blockquote
                %p
                  It is widely conjectured that the
                  %a{:href => "universality+class#GeneralAnd2DCriticalPhenomena"} critical limit
                  of interfaces of statistical models, such as hull percolations and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ising+model"} Ising
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+walls"} domain walls
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+invariance"} conformally-invariant
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
                  (CFT). Using the technology from CFT, we will propose the closed expression for a large class of three-point connectivities of interfaces in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "universality+class#GeneralAnd2DCriticalPhenomena"} 2D critical statistical models
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Temperley-Lieb+algebra"} Temperley-Lieb algebra
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brownian+loop+soup"} loop ensembles
                  by Xin Sun al. Up to our best knowledge, this is one of the first instances where we have a non-trivial agreement between
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brownian+loop+soup"} conformal loop ensembles
          %p
